    dc:type "resolution-route/empirical-data";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: For a corpus with known provenance, estimate whether systems are minimal for selected features and compare minimality distributions between designed and natural systems. Likelihood ratios could test minimality as evidence of purpose, but not establish purpose with certainty or extrapolate to advanced extraterrestrial technology.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Global minimality is generally uncomputable or search-space dependent.", "Known artifact corpora poorly represent advanced technology.", "Natural selection can also produce optimization.";
